                <pb facs="0501" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg489"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3531/1524: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Armour</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-06-06T16:00:00-04:00">June 6, 1940—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>93. Department’s telegram no. 81 of May 29, 6 p.m. Please telegraph any reaction
                    so far expressed by Argentine officials to the proposal contained in
                    Department’s 79<anchor n="29" xml:id="d572-f1"/> regarding possible coordination
                    of corn marketing activity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
